🔹 Program 10: Base Reference With a Virtual Function

📌 Description

This program demonstrates run-time polymorphism using a base-class reference.

A "Shape" reference can refer to different derived objects such as "Rectangle" and "Circle".

Because "area()" is virtual, the correct derived implementation is called at run time.

🎯 Concept Used

Run-Time Polymorphism — Base Reference

💡 Key Point

Passing an object using "const Base&" preserves the actual derived object and enables virtual function dispatch.
